{#
settings/_sidebar_more.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Which of the sidebar's system folders wait behind "More".

One box per folder, ticked when the folder is behind More — so the page opens
showing exactly what the sidebar shows, and the default (Snoozed, Archive, Spam
and Trash) is simply what is ticked until somebody changes it.

The Inbox is not offered: it stays on top whatever anybody chooses, and says so
rather than being silently missing from the list. See SidebarRow::isPinned().

Checkboxes rather than the On/Off segment the booleans on this page wear,
because this is a list of eight questions with one answer each, not one
question; the calendar editor's list of calendars is the same shape and the same
control. Each change submits on its own (ui--auto-submit), like every control
here, so there is no Save to forget.

The hidden `rows[]` entry is always posted. A form with every box cleared would
otherwise post no `rows` at all, which is indistinguishable from a post that
did not mention them — and "nothing behind More" is a choice that has to be
storable. See SidebarMoreController.

This is only WHERE a folder is drawn. Hiding one altogether is the eye toggle in
Labels, which the note says, because the two are easy to confuse and a person
looking for the second will find the first.
#}
{% set behind = app.user.sidebarMoreRows %}

<form method="post"
      action="{{ path('app_settings_sidebar_more_update') }}"
      data-turbo="false"
      data-controller="ui--auto-submit"
      class="px-4 py-3">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-sidebar') }}">
    <input type="hidden" name="rows[]" value="">

    <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.sidebar.label'|trans }}</legend>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5 mb-2">{{ 'settings.sidebar.hint'|trans }}</p>

        <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            {% for row in enum('App\\Domain\\Enum\\Mail\\SidebarRow').cases()|filter(r => not r.isPinned) %}
                <li>
                    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-ink cursor-pointer">
                        <input type="checkbox"
                               name="rows[]"
                               value="{{ row.value }}"
                               {{ row in behind ? 'checked' : '' }}
                               data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                               class="rounded border-line accent-accent focus:ring-accent">
                        <span>{{ ('sidebar.nav.' ~ row.value)|trans }}</span>
                    </label>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </fieldset>

    <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-3">
        {{ 'settings.sidebar.pinned'|trans }}
        {{ 'settings.sidebar.hide_note'|trans }}
    </p>
</form>
